        question: "Why can't you just stucco an adobe building with cement stucco?",
        answer: "Because cement stucco is rigid and nearly vapor-closed, while adobe needs to flex slightly and to dry to the outside. Cement stucco traps moisture inside the wall, where it softens the adobe and rots the mortar — the wall looks fine until it fails. The correct finishes are lime-based plasters and mineral paints that bond with the earthen wall, move with it, and let moisture pass through. This is the most common and most destructive mistake in adobe work.",
