        question: "How much rain does a desert roof drainage system handle?",
        answer: "The design is based on the cloudburst intensity the plumbing code requires — the inches-per-hour rate of a severe monsoon storm — not the desert's modest annual rainfall. A flat commercial roof can see thousands of gallons arriving in minutes during a cloudburst, which is why the code requires both primary drains sized for that intensity and overflow protection set above them. The engineer also verifies the structure can carry the ponded water if the primaries clog.",
