        heading: "Arizona HVAC Dust Control Checklist",
        body: "Use this checklist before the HVAC drawings are issued:\n\n• Filter efficiency selected per occupancy, with pre-filters protecting final filters\n• Fans selected for loaded-filter pressure drop; dirty-filter alarms programmed at specified setpoints\n• Building air balance calculated for positive pressurization with every exhaust accounted for\n• Envelope air barrier, penetration sealing, and door weatherstripping detailed on the drawings\n• High-traffic entries given vestibules, air curtains, or interlocked doors\n• Ductwork specified to sealed construction with leakage testing\n• Outdoor equipment protected: coil coatings, elevated or screened installation, haboob recirculation sequence\n• Dust-season filter-maintenance schedule, coil-cleaning intervals, and storm-response procedure in the O&M manual\n• Adopted energy code edition confirmed for the jurisdiction; filtration and sealing provisions coordinated",
