        answer: "Far more than most owners expect — an uncovered pool in 110-degree heat with low humidity and wind can lose a quarter inch or more of water depth per day, which over a large resort pool is thousands of gallons daily, carrying away heat and chemicals with it. The engineer prepares an evaporation budget during design so the owner sees the number, then designs covers, wind screening, and operating schedules against it. Evaporation control is usually the highest-return investment in the pool's mechanical design.",
