        question: "Why is a church sanctuary harder to cool than an office?",
        answer: "The occupancy swings harder and the acoustic demands are stricter. An office holds a steady headcount all week; a sanctuary goes from empty to five hundred people in half an hour, then back to empty — so the system must pull down fast, handle the full people-load, and do it all whisper-quiet for prayer and music. Offices tolerate background HVAC noise that would ruin a worship service. The engineer designs for the transient load and the noise criteria together.",
